  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Establishing an ICT-Integrated Earthquake Response Platform in the Philippines (`24-`26 /1.68 billion won)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In order to prevent natural disasters (earthquakes, typhoons, etc.) and social disasters (collapse of buildings, etc.) in advance, measuring equipment (integrated seismometer, wind direction/wind speed gauge, etc.) is installed in facilities provided by Philippine government agencies and collected from the measuring equipment Building a digital disaster response network to strengthen the disaster response capabilities of the Philippines and Metro Manila from various disasters by collecting, storing, and analyzing the collected data to conduct a safety evaluation of facilities and displaying the results in the integrated control platform.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reduction human and material damage caused by natural and social disasters by installing measurement equipment (earthquakes, typhoons, hazardous facilities) and an Total management platform for the disasters in major buildings in Metro Manila, which are highly vulnerable to natural disasters, and have real-time disaster response capabilities at the local and national level and advancementICT &#xae30;&#xbc18; &#xd544;&#xb9ac;&#xd540; &#xba54;&#xd2b8;&#xb85c;&#xb9c8;&#xb2d0;&#xb77c; &#xc9c0;&#xc9c4;&#xb300;&#xc751;&#xb825; &#xac15;&#xd654; &#xd14c;&#xc2a4;&#xd2b8; &#xd1b5;&#xacfc;</narrative>
  </description>
